From: Radxa Sky1 <linux-sky1@radxa.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: install CoreSight ETE SSDT for ACPI-booted CIX SKY1

CIX Orion O6 firmware boots Linux via ACPI but exposes neither
ACPI Processor() devices for the 12 cores nor any CoreSight nodes.
Without ACPI namespace processor objects, per_cpu(processors) stays
NULL and the in-tree etm4x ACPI binding (which finds the parent CPU
via acpi_get_parent + acpi_handle_to_logical_cpuid) cannot resolve
a logical CPU for ETE devices.

Embed and dynamically install a small SSDT that declares 12
\_SB.CPUx ACPI0007 processor devices (UID 0..11 matching MADT GICC)
each with an ARMHC500 ETE child. The standard ACPI processor driver
populates per_cpu(processors), then the etm4x platform driver binds
the ETE children and registers one CoreSight ETE source per CPU.

Sinks (TMC ETF/ETR), dynamic funnel, STM and TRBE are NOT included:
their drivers in 6.6.x lack ACPI match tables. Trace data has no
sink yet; this patch only gets ETE sources visible under
/sys/bus/coresight/devices/. Sink ACPI support will be a follow-up.

Signed-off-by: Radxa Sky1 <linux-sky1@radxa.com>
---
 src/drivers/acpi/Makefile         |   2 +
 src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c | 103 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 105 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c

--- a/src/drivers/acpi/Makefile
+++ b/src/drivers/acpi/Makefile
@@ -133,2 +133,4 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_ACPI_VIOT)		+= viot.o
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_RISCV)		+= riscv/
+
+obj-$(CONFIG_ARCH_CIX)		+= sky1-coresight.o
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c
@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * sky1-coresight: install a CoreSight ETE SSDT at boot on CIX SKY1.
+ *
+ * Orion O6 firmware exposes no ACPI nodes for CoreSight components and
+ * also no ACPI Processor() devices for the 12 CPU cores (CPUs come
+ * solely from MADT GICC entries). This driver installs an SSDT that
+ * declares ACPI0007 processor devices and ARMHC500 ETE children so the
+ * in-tree etm4x driver can bind one ETE per CPU.
+ *
+ * Sinks (TMC ETF/ETR), dynamic funnel, STM and TRBE are intentionally
+ * absent: their drivers in this kernel lack ACPI match tables. Trace
+ * routing remains unavailable until those are backported; this patch
+ * provides the foundation by getting per-CPU ETE devices registered.
+ */
